small_email: Zombie-style proximity policy on Enron email.

Policy, faithful to Zombie (NSDI'24) §6.3 proximity example:
  keyword within 300 chars of number_arm, case-sensitive, dot-all,
  BOTH directions (F = keyword.{0,300}arm, B = arm.{0,300}keyword).
  5 SIT families, one primary keyword each, F+B pair = 10 DLP sigs.

  Family       primary kw        number arm
  -----------  ----------------  -----------------------
  Passport     passport          [0-9a-zA-Z][0-9]{8}
  SSN          SSN               [0-9]{3}[-\s]?[0-9]{2}?[-\s]?[0-9]{4}
  License      driving license   ([0-9]{3}\s){2}[0-9]{3}
  Bank         bank account      [0-9]{6,17}
  ITIN         ITIN              9[0-9]{2}[-\s]?(5[0-9]|6[0-5]|..)[-\s]?[0-9]{4}

main_dfa.dat lists ONLY the Win.Alphabet.SAMPLE-1 seed sig (cheap
hex DFA that seeds the 16-nibble alphabet). The 10 DLP sigs are NOT
in the DFA list -- building a DFA for the .{0,300} x 5-arm union is
too expensive; they go through the SED / pm-bounds path instead.

Scan target: data/samples/email_merged128k/merged_000020. It has
the keyword (x2) and the License "ddd ddd ddd" arm (x6) but no arm
match within 300 chars of a keyword -> clean under all 10 arms ->
discharges green while exercising the proximity prune.

Run: cargo test -p zkregplus -- test_small_email \
       --show-output --nocapture
